# Declarative map of every credential the protected release lanes need.
#
# FORMAT (whitespace separated, four columns):
#   <github-environment>  <secret-name>  <1password-reference>  <required|optional>
#
# The 1Password reference is an `op://<vault>/<item>/<field>` secret reference.
# Item titles below were confirmed to exist by --discover. The FIELD names are
# still placeholders: run `./tooling/provision-release-secrets.sh --fields` to
# print the real labels, then replace each `<field>` here.
#
# NOTHING IN THIS FILE IS A CREDENTIAL. It names where credentials live, not
# what they are. It is committed deliberately so the credential surface of this
# repository is reviewable in the tree.
#
# Note the item titles use an EN DASH, matching 1Password exactly. A hyphen
# will not resolve.

recovery-protected  KEEPLING_BACKUP_PRIMARY_ENDPOINT    op://Personal/Keepling – B2 Primary Backup/<field>       required
recovery-protected  KEEPLING_BACKUP_PRIMARY_REGION      op://Personal/Keepling – B2 Primary Backup/<field>       required
recovery-protected  KEEPLING_BACKUP_PRIMARY_ACCESS_KEY  op://Personal/Keepling – B2 Primary Backup/<field>       required
recovery-protected  KEEPLING_BACKUP_PRIMARY_SECRET_KEY  op://Personal/Keepling – B2 Primary Backup/<field>       required

recovery-live       HCLOUD_TOKEN                        op://Personal/Keepling – Hetzner Provisioning/<field>    required
recovery-live       CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN                op://Personal/Keepling – Cloudflare DNS Cutover/<field>  required
recovery-live       KEEPLING_DNS_ZONE_ID                op://Personal/Keepling – Cloudflare DNS Cutover/<field>  required
recovery-live       KEEPLING_DNS_RECORD_NAME            op://Personal/Keepling – Cloudflare DNS Cutover/<field>  required
